"derivative","format":"512Kb MPEG4","original":"brief_city_TNA_56K.wmv","md5":"4d7c3cf7a67e0a182aa1f10f30bb578f","mtime":"1227457230","size":"80263577","crc32":"01c1bac1","sha1":"b47f859e8e0485674f9f80295b36fcd53facf4f0","length":"1123.38","height":"240","width":"320"},{"name":"brief_city_TNA_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"513b0ffca270173cfc706e8811cf813e1528b3ff","mtime":"1547521899","size":"38288","md5":"0b94e09d3534c87264605e5ec20fc8d4","crc32":"7f0f8bc6","sha1":"103c650ede612b2acca6e42a894e4cafa79352b1","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"brief_city_TNA_files.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","md5":"b3af08456d5265a9883b99d2273c1e35","summation":"md5"},{"name":"brief_city_TNA_meta.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1547521877","size":"1247","md5":"573eb017247e811f9f3021fcdba4b820","crc32":"e7848433","sha1":"1ff1ce101241c3946e66b36207cfba2b54ce85b5"},{"name":"brief_city_TNA_reviews.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1348785306","size":"2111","md5":"192ca8881be74a41b856a8720662d1b3","crc32":"fd7c68a0","sha1":"06ec8aba40973861e345590e75ea70cfe0baccd9"}],"files_count":74,"item_last_updated":1708584005,"item_size":1818608059,"metadata":{"identifier":"brief_city_TNA","title":"Brief City","mediatype":"movies","collection":["british_gov_public_films","ephemera"],"subject":"Festival; Britain South Bank Exhibition; design; architecture","description":"A retrospective view of the 1951 Festival of Britain on the South Bank with special reference to design and architecture","date":"1952","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-07 10:47:37","addeddate":"2005-10-07 17:47:13","uploader":"florian@archive.org","sponsor":"Central Office of Information and The Observer","director":"Maurice Harvey, Jacques Brunius","publisher":"Massingham Productions Ltd","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"18:44","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","updatedate":"2005-10-07 10:49:51","updater":"nVIR","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"18 Minutes 44 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"I have enjoyed this one on DVD, primarily to look closely at the great detail of this amazing 1951 fair-exhibition.  Pro camerawork, requires swapping PAL 24 frames to NTSC 30 frames to burn to disk here in the USA.  We are observing the healing process for England after the devastation of WWII. Very highly recommended for anyone involved in architecture and design.","reviewtitle":"Worth watching, despite garbeled soundtrack","stars":"4","reviewer":"Visual16","createdate":"2006-09-22 23:56:04","reviewdate":"2006-09-22 23:56:04"},{"reviewbody":"Interesting film here about an exposition in London. Seems like the main focus was to distract Londoners from their droll and mundane lives in England. It certainly SOUNDSS that way in the narration. Were things THAT bad in England in the late 40's??","reviewtitle":"hurray.","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-05-22 00:57:32","createdate":"2008-05-22 00:57:32","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"Apart from the wobbly music [understandable], the film quality is very good for the time, and allowing for the fact that nightime filming with natural light, was a problem.\n\nI thought that making the two men the sort of, focus, was a good idea.  I enjoyed the narration, but most of all, the social history.  As I was seven at the time, my memory was stirred concerning the people, the way they dressed and comported themselves and the little boys with their caps and their short trousers.  And yes, ordinary people did behave themselves.","reviewtitle":"Social history","reviewer":"mendacious","reviewdate":"2012-09-27 22:34:59","createdate":"2012-09-27 22:34:59","stars":"5"}],"server":"dn601201.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn601201":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5432090489"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-12 01:57:03.394216"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":987443887,"workable_servers":["dn601201.us.archive.org"]}